Yeah...

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:29.880
Urushi!

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.670
Come on, get those feet moving!

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.920
The temples are waiting for us!

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.290
Okay, okay!

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.830
This is gonna be fun!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.830
<b>Love</b>

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.830
<b>Fortune</b>

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.460
You're doing it, Urushi!

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:53.670
Oh, that way! That way!

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:56.000
Whew, I did it!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.710
Nice work, Urushi!

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.330
And the last spot on our love tour is...

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.630
Shimogamo Shrine!

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:04.790
Yeah!

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.290
Urushi!

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.540
Make sure to pray to the love gods.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.460
Oh yeah! I was having so much fun, I totally forgot!

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.380
I pray for fulfillment in love...

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:29.000
No, I'm pretty sure it's just that Ayumu likes me...

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.250
I don't necessarily like him back.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:44.330
I don't know if this prayer will actually work, but
I pray that Ayumu will get much, much better at shogi.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.290
Whew, we went everywhere.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.250
I guess it's time we go back to the hotel.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.750
How can you say that!?

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.580
You know this isn't over yet!

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.790
There's still one more thing we have to do!

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:09.830
Of course! We're at Shimogamo Shrine! That's...

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.130
The birthplace of mitarashi dango!

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:13.170
It is?

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:15.330
Ladies! Let's go!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.250
Yeah!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.210
Hey, wait for me!

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:23.500
<b>Shogi Club</b>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:23.500
<b>Urushi Yaotome</b>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:23.500
<b>Ayumu Tanaka</b>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:23.500
<b>Takeru Kakuryu</b>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:23.500
<b>Rin Kagawa</b>

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:23.080
Thanks for your help last night.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.630
It was no trouble. Don't worry about it.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.080
Let me do something to thank you.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.210
I can buy you pork buns-

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:31.040
Pork!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.000
I want something big and meaty!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.380
Maybe that's a little too greedy of me?

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:41.330
You get so excited when food is involved.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.830
Please stop talking about me like I'm a glutton.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:50.210
Anyway, do you ever get excited
about anything, Tanaka-san?

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:53.250
I'm human, like everyone else. It happens.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.330
Really? I can't imagine it.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.330
What are you like when you're excited?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:03.540
I put both hands up in the air.

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:09.290
You're like a wild animal...

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.460
Urushi!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.580
What? You were awake?

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:24.330
What's wrong? You look so lonely.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.130
I-I do not.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.080
And you're heavy.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:29.380
How rude.

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.830
Seriously, nothing is wrong.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.000
Then you want to play shogi with me?

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.290
I can't believe I'm actually playing shogi with you, Maki.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:51.210
Let's see... So the gold can't go diagonally backwards...

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:53.170
So I'll do this.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.500
So what made you actually want to play?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.170
Just a whim.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.460
Well, fine. I finally get to play again, so I'm gonna enjoy it.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.290
Then next I'll do this!

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:11.960
Did I do something wrong?

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.500
Oh, sorry. It isn't that.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:18.580
I was just thinking, when Ayumu started playing shogi,
he was like that, too.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:23.210
But he got better so fast.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.580
He learned how all the pieces move in no time,
and he just kept improving.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:28.830
Hey, Urushi.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:33.500
Are you sure you don't like Tanaka-kun?

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.710
I-I told you, I don't!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.580
And why do you care so much anyway?

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.790
It just makes me happy.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.080
To think that maybe you're
finally experiencing your first love.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.250
Well, I'm sorry.

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.040
For giving you the wrong idea.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:58.830
Maybe sometimes people just don't realize it, and then
suddenly it hits them, "Oh! I like them!" It could happen.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.130
Y-you really think so?

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.000
I dunno.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.420
You're just making stuff up!

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:08.290
But when it does happen to you, make sure to tell me!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.960
I'll do everything I can to help things work out!

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:16.250
No. I won't tell you.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.290
What.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.460
Why not!? You have to tell me!

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.040
Because it's embarrassing!

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.580
Well, I think that's enough for tonight.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:34.710
Yeah.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.630
Feeling better?

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.750
Yeah, a lot better.

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:40.960
Shogi really is the best.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:48.000
Thank you, Maki.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.170
You're very welcome.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:55.580
Not that playing shogi with me will
help you feel any less lonely.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:57.750
Did you say something?

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.250
Nope! Good night!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.710
<b>How's it going?</b>

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.830
<b>Send</b>

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:22.420
So it would be more beneficial to go with the rook on 69.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:24.920
There's also potential to turn it into a Paperweight castle.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:26.460
I see...

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:29.880
It's getting late.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:32.330
Yes. Would you like to call it a night, then?

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:36.250
Thanks. I appreciate you staying up to help me.

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:39.500
Tanaka-san.

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.670
When you beat Ms. President...

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.960
You're going to tell her how you feel about her, right?

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.000
Yes.

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.330
You really do like her, don't you?

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:53.580
I'm in love.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.080
Rin?

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.460
It's nothing! Anyway, good night.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:10.830
Oh, man!

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:23.130
What was that about?

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.000
<b>Senpai</b>

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.000
<b>How's it going?</b>

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.130
These dango are deee-lish!

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:41.830
Yeah! And they taste even better
when you're wearing a kimono!

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.920
This is so school trip.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:46.080
You look really good in yours, Urushi!

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:48.960
Urushi?

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:51.960
Uh, right! We do have to buy souvenirs!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.630
What are you talking about?

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:58.960
Is it just me, or have you been up in la-la land all day?

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:01.000
Did something happen?

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:03.250
No, nothing special.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.210
Really?

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.500
Really!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:11.920
Hey, Urushi!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.750
Yes! That's a good one!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.000
Tell me what happened!

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:21.830
Or else my hand will slip, and this photo
will be sent straight to you-know-who.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.830
N-no, you can't do that!

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.580
I have bean jam on my face! It's too embarrassing!

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:30.170
Then tell me.

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.750
I know it has something to do with Tanaka-kun!

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.130
Okay, fine.

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.380
I have not been up in la-la land, but well...

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:46.580
I mean, when I woke up and checked my phone
this morning, I had a text from Ayumu.

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:48.830
And, um...

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:52.580
Tonight... he's going to call me.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.460
Ah, the joys of youth!

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.830
That's great!

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.210
I'm so happy for you, Urushi!

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:07.500
Well, the class representatives have a meeting,
so I'll excuse myself early today.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:08.330
Alright.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.790
Here. I made a notebook listing all your weaknesses.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:14.710
You did this for me?

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:16.540
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.420
Have a good day.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:24.580
There's so much here...

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:40.380
Takeru?

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:43.460
Oh, hi Ayumu. So what? Club's already over?

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.210
Rin left early.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:47.460
I wasn't afraid of her, okay!

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:50.710
I had library duty yesterday!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:53.880
Wanna play?

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:55.630
Y-yeah.

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:02.790
Tonight...

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.080
I have plans to talk to Senpai on the phone.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.250
Wow, good for you!

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:10.580
Yeah.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.670
So what are you gonna talk to her about?

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:15.000
We're going to play shogi.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.630
Ugh, shogi again? Not exactly romantic.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:23.710
What do you talk about when
you call Sakurako on the phone?

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:26.250
Th-this has nothing to do with me!

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:28.710
So...

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:32.920
Why are you making me wear a yukata?

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:35.670
You're having a late-night rendezvous with a man.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.540
You gotta wear a yukata!

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:39.880
It's a phonecall. He won't see it.

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.830
Apparently it's what he can't see that matters most.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.130
Urushi!

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:48.920
I heard that when he says,
"The moon is beautiful," it means, "I love you."

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:51.250
Make sure to remember that.

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:54.040
You can be the one to say it, too.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:55.540
Neither of us is gonna say it!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.960
I'm just playing a game of shogi with a boy from my club!

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:58.960
Of course, of course.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.500
Are you listening to me?

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:01.830
Yes, I'm listening.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:08.670
Okay. Well, I'm going now.

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:10.250
Urushi!

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:13.130
You can do it!

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:15.250
You didn't listen to a word I said!

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:23.380
Ugh, they had to say all that weird stuff.

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:25.250
Now I'm nervous!

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:29.170
Five more minutes...

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:05.000
The term "next to" is surprisingly versatile

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:11.960
For example, you can be one meter apart
from someone and still be "next to" them

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:20.040
We're in a stale-mate, in a town dyed rosy red

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:28.960
I want to know your real feelings, but you evade and keep walking

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:38.540
Then I realize we're within 50 centimeters (doo-wop x2)

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:46.250
Or am I outside of 50 centimeters? (doo-wop x2)

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:53.670
What is the reason we walk home together? (doo-wop x2)

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:57.960
Unable to ask, our shadows align
